{"id": "police-retirees-rehired-960", "title": "Rehired retirees: police use of the 960 program quadrupled to $11.4 million", "seconds": 134.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "tempo": 1.12, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "20b8681a2ab763b1", "words": 423, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "The City’s Charter lets it rehire its own retirees for special skills, while they keep their pension.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.23, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“requiring special skills or knowledge”"}, "emph": ["special skills"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.49, 0.9, 1.12, 1.22, 1.72, 1.9, 2.1, 2.64, 2.78, 3.11, 3.92, 4.1, 4.24, 4.46, 4.61]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "The cap is 120 working days or 960 hours a year, whichever is greater.", "t0": 5.35, "t1": 9.48, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“120 working days or 960 hours, whichever is greater, in any one fiscal year”"}, "emph": ["960 hours"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.51, 0.73, 0.91, 1.15, 1.41, 1.71, 1.96, 2.08, 2.24, 2.46, 2.74, 2.99, 3.07, 3.29, 3.64, 3.75]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 9.6, "t1": 10.79, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.28, 0.36, 0.6, 0.74, 0.81]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "dn"], "text": "The Police Department calls it the 960 Program. What did it pay in fiscal 2026?", "t0": 11.01, "t1": 16.76, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "The 960 Program", "kicker": "Police Department", "sub": "each rehire approved by the Chief"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.41, 0.81, 1.07, 1.17, 1.31, 1.55, 1.85, 2.19, 3.14, 3.33, 3.45, 3.56, 3.82, 3.94, 4.28, 4.52]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "11.4 million dollars, to 249 payroll rows.", "t0": 16.76, "t1": 20.39, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$11.4 million", "label": "paid to 249 rehired-retiree rows, fiscal 2026", "sub": "$11,446,151"}, "emph": ["11.4 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.37, 0.59, 0.8, 1.08, 1.75, 1.92, 2.1, 2.35, 2.81, 3.2]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "line", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "trajectory"], "text": "In fiscal 2022 it was 61 rows and 2.3 million dollars. It quadrupled in four years.", "t0": 20.91, "t1": 26.74, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "line", "series": [0], "kicker": "Pay to rehired-retiree Police Officer 3 rows, fiscal 2017 to 2026", "from": "FY2017", "to": "FY2026"}, "emph": ["quadrupled"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.47, 0.69, 1.3, 1.43, 1.57, 2.11, 2.47, 2.61, 2.86, 3.1, 3.32, 3.6, 4.45, 4.61, 5.11, 5.21, 5.44]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "On the payroll they are Police Officer 3 rows, temporary exempt, with no City retirement cost.", "t0": 26.86, "t1": 32.37, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "How they show on the payroll", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Police Officer 3", "sub": "class Q004"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Temporary exempt", "sub": "not a permanent post"}, {"art": "money", "name": "No City retirement cost", "sub": "the rehired-retiree profile"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.25, 0.61, 0.73, 0.86, 1.18, 1.56, 1.82, 2.53, 3.05, 3.74, 3.97, 4.15, 4.4, 4.83]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Do their names appear in the Retirement System’s 2022 pension list?", "t0": 32.49, "t1": 36.33, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Names in the 2022 pension list", "kicker": "Retirement System", "sub": "258 temporary-exempt Police Officer 3 rows, fiscal 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.34, 0.57, 0.92, 1.0, 1.09, 1.54, 1.95, 2.22, 2.65, 3.0]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "210 of 258 do. Shuffled names match about 11.", "t0": 36.33, "t1": 40.58, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["names in the pension list", "210 of 258"], "b": ["with first names shuffled", "about 11"]}, "emph": ["210"], "wt": [0.04, 0.26, 0.53, 0.78, 0.88, 1.08, 1.33, 2.11, 2.47, 2.86, 3.17, 3.41, 3.62]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "With no member number, a name match can’t show if it’s the same person or two people.", "t0": 41.0, "t1": 44.53, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A name match does not show whether a row is the same person."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.34, 0.59, 0.92, 1.04, 1.23, 1.46, 1.69, 1.91, 2.02, 2.17, 2.28, 2.51, 2.89, 3.04, 3.21]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "bla"], "text": "In May 2024, the Board’s Budget and Legislative Analyst reported on the Airport Bureau.", "t0": 44.75, "t1": 49.32, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "report of 10 May 2024, File 24-0331"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.43, 0.67, 1.47, 1.62, 1.92, 2.25, 2.38, 2.92, 3.32, 3.7, 3.79, 3.88, 4.22]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[3]"], "text": "It found about 38 retirees helping to backfill vacant positions.", "t0": 49.44, "t1": 53.06, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“the Airport Bureau is using approximately 38 retirees to help backfill vacant positions”"}, "emph": ["backfill vacant positions"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.47, 0.73, 1.23, 1.83, 2.12, 2.23, 2.71, 3.0]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[3]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "37 were Community Ambassadors. The analyst wrote that they are not sworn officers.", "t0": 53.18, "t1": 57.94, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "37", "label": "served as Community Ambassadors", "sub": "“not considered sworn officers”"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.62, 0.77, 1.16, 2.34, 2.52, 2.88, 3.12, 3.26, 3.4, 3.53, 3.69, 4.03]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[2]"], "text": "Yet the Charter says the work shall not replace a permanent civil service employee.", "t0": 58.06, "t1": 61.57, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“shall not replace a permanent civil service employee”"}, "emph": ["shall not replace"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.29, 0.59, 0.81, 0.92, 1.08, 1.27, 1.41, 1.77, 1.85, 2.22, 2.49, 2.79]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Does filling vacant posts square with that? The analyst cited the Charter section, but not that rule.", "t0": 61.69, "t1": 66.66, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Backfilling vacant positions", "sub": "the analyst cited the section, not this rule"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.5, 0.8, 1.07, 1.34, 1.46, 2.39, 2.57, 2.94, 3.18, 3.28, 3.57, 4.13, 4.32, 4.48, 4.68]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].what"], "text": "Now the hours. In fiscal 2026, 54 of the 249 rows passed 960 hours.", "t0": 66.88, "t1": 73.28, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "54 of 249", "label": "rehired-retiree rows above 960 hours, fiscal 2026", "sub": "8 of 61 in fiscal 2022"}, "emph": ["54"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.36, 1.36, 1.55, 1.92, 2.18, 2.9, 3.48, 3.57, 3.66, 3.8, 4.03, 4.48, 4.8, 5.12, 5.31, 5.54, 5.85]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[0]"], "text": "None passed 1,200 hours, in any year since fiscal 2017.", "t0": 73.4, "t1": 77.65, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "0", "label": "rows with this profile above 1,200 hours", "sub": "fiscal 2017 to 2026"}, "emph": ["None"], "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.64, 0.83, 1.17, 1.33, 1.55, 2.17, 2.35, 2.59, 2.81, 3.04, 3.42, 3.68]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why", "innocent[2]"], "text": "Why 1,200? Ten-hour days make 120 working days 1,200 hours.", "t0": 78.07, "t1": 83.1, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["960 hours", "the hours cap"], "b": ["120 days of 10 hours", "1,200 hours"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.45, 0.78, 0.96, 1.66, 2.09, 2.35, 2.55, 2.73, 2.96, 3.26, 3.54, 3.75, 3.91, 4.25, 4.4, 4.63]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Citywide, 277 people who retired in 2018 to 2022 worked for the City again.", "t0": 83.32, "t1": 88.99, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "277", "label": "of 3,931 people who retired in 2018 to 2022", "sub": "paid again by fiscal 2026: $34,308,211"}, "emph": ["277"], "wt": [0.0, 0.74, 0.97, 1.26, 1.85, 2.12, 2.27, 2.61, 2.71, 2.97, 3.3, 3.39, 3.64, 4.62, 4.9, 5.02, 5.12, 5.36]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].where", "established[5]"], "text": "This match adds a second key: the payroll shows each one leaving at retirement.", "t0": 89.11, "t1": 93.09, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "A second key", "sub": "the payroll shows each one leaving at the retirement date"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.5, 0.79, 0.88, 1.19, 1.96, 2.1, 2.48, 2.74, 2.96, 3.15, 3.44, 3.53]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Their median was 571 hours a year, well under 960.", "t0": 93.21, "t1": 97.13, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "571", "label": "median hours a year", "sub": "858 person-years"}, "emph": ["571"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.5, 0.65, 0.9, 1.14, 1.57, 1.82, 1.91, 2.42, 2.66, 2.87, 3.07, 3.32]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "The Sheriff shows the same profile, smaller:", "t0": 97.25, "t1": 100.26, "shot": "b21s", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Sheriff, fiscal 2022", "7 rows"], "b": ["Sheriff, fiscal 2026", "38 rows"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.41, 0.7, 0.8, 1.03, 1.73]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "7 deputy rows in fiscal 2022, 38 in fiscal 2026.", "t0": 100.26, "t1": 104.93, "shot": "b21s", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Sheriff, fiscal 2022", "7 rows"], "b": ["Sheriff, fiscal 2026", "38 rows"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["38"], "wt": [0.04, 0.35, 0.66, 0.94, 1.08, 1.44, 1.71, 2.79, 3.31, 3.44, 3.75, 3.97]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "pen"], "text": "The public pension list covers only 2022, last updated in November 2023.", "t0": 105.15, "t1": 110.16, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "pen", "kicker": "Retiree Pensions Annual Benefit Received · last updated 8 November 2023", "text": "Tax year 2022 only · 28,993 rows · no member number", "mark": "no member number"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.42, 0.75, 0.98, 1.27, 1.47, 1.76, 2.95, 3.25, 3.65, 3.75, 4.18, 4.46]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "The Department’s own 960 Program audits are not published.", "t0": 110.28, "t1": 113.98, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“The SDU will conduct audits of the 960 Program and generate status reports for the Chief of Police”"}, "emph": ["not published"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.59, 0.86, 1.08, 1.36, 1.75, 2.21, 2.62, 2.82, 3.01]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Nothing here shows that any retiree passed the cap, or replaced a permanent officer.", "t0": 114.2, "t1": 118.42, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any retiree passed the Charter cap", "That any rehire replaced a permanent officer", "Whether a payroll row is the same person as a pensioner of the same name"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.46, 0.8, 0.95, 1.15, 1.62, 1.9, 1.99, 2.82, 2.99, 3.35, 3.43, 3.77]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "innocent[1]"], "text": "A rehire also costs less: the City pays no pension contribution on that work.", "t0": 118.54, "t1": 122.78, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "A rehire costs less", "sub": "no pension contribution on the pay"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.64, 0.9, 1.21, 2.05, 2.19, 2.43, 2.68, 2.82, 3.13, 3.66, 3.75, 3.91]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it?", "t0": 122.9, "t1": 123.96, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The 960 Program status reports, fiscal 2023 to 2026"}, {"who": "", "what": "Re-employed retirees by member number, with hours"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.29, 0.56]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "The 960 Program status reports, and the Retirement System’s counts by member number.", "t0": 123.96, "t1": 128.67, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The 960 Program status reports, fiscal 2023 to 2026"}, {"who": "", "what": "Re-employed retirees by member number, with hours"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.04, 0.21, 0.39, 0.62, 0.93, 1.28, 1.63, 2.48, 2.64, 2.74, 3.15, 3.52, 3.84, 4.01, 4.25]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has found that any retiree passed the cap.", "t0": 128.79, "t1": 131.44, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.62, 0.76, 0.97, 1.12, 1.36, 1.85, 2.15, 2.25]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 131.56, "t1": 133.33, "shot": "b29", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.34, 0.44, 0.52, 0.9, 1.06, 1.15]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The rule", "lead1": "Lead 1 · 61 rows to 249", "lead2": "Lead 2 · backfilling vacancies", "lead3": "Lead 3 · the hours", "lead4": "Lead 4 · citywide", "lead5": "Lead 5 · the record stops at 2022", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "document"}